# LinuxMumble ships to Linux: every text file MUST check out with LF endings,
# even on a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true. A stray CRLF in install.sh or
# the generated `mumble` launcher breaks the "#!/usr/bin/env bash" shebang on
# Linux ("bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M"). Python tolerates CRLF, but we
# normalize everything to LF for consistency.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
